From bbe99ab04b5fb2c7aefde3f1d43c1028ee9aee9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:42:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Screenshot] Shift+Print Screen saves the frame of the
 video

Issue #30. The frame of the video alone, at its own size where it can be
had so (the commit before), is saved by:

- Shift+Print Screen (keyboard.xml, next to Print Screen, which saves
  the screen as before);
- "Save the frame of the video", a button in the video settings of the
  player, next to "Set as default for all media", for a remote;
- TakeScreenshot(video) and GUI.TakeScreenshot with "video", which took
  the video at the size it is drawn.

CScreenShot::TakeVideoFrame() asks for the capture first, so that the
frame on the screen is the one taken; the folder, the name and the
writing come after, on the worker of the capture service, never on the
thread that draws. It is saved in the screenshot folder as
videoNNNNN.png, numbered after the frames already there, or into the
file or folder given to the builtin, and written as a screenshot is: an
HDR frame in PQ or HLG, tagged so (cICP), with its SDR copy beside it
(videoNNNNN-sdr.png, as 1.2 makes it), an SDR frame tagged sRGB.

kodi.log says at INFO what was saved, its size and whether it is the
video's own, how it was taken and how long it held the thread that
draws; a notice says "Video frame saved" with the name and the size
("at the size it is shown" where it is not its own), or "No video frame
saved" and why: no video plays, the picture cannot be captured as it is
shown now (kodi.log says why), or the file could not be written.

The help of "Screenshot folder" (System > Logging) says both keys.
English first; es_es, es_ar and es_mx translated (core 62860 to 62867,
Estuary 54860 to 54867).
